{
  "repo": "ARMOR-NODE-ALARM",
  "ecosystem": "armor",
  "tagline": "An alarm panel that decides by itself: zones, delays, PIN, siren and a Zigbee link that takes over when the server is gone; it is not a certified alarm system.",
  "description": "The firmware of ARMOR-NODE-ALARM reads up to eight wired loops, turns them into zone states, runs the rules of the panel (arming, delays, alarm, silence, PIN with lockout) and drives its own siren relay. The state is kept in flash across restarts. Nothing has run on a board or in a real installation.",
  "columns": [
    "WHAT IS CONNECTED",
    "THIS FIRMWARE",
    "WHO IT TALKS TO"
  ],
